<header class="main-header">
  <div class="series-title">Likutay Halachos &middot; Choshen Mishpat</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Eidus 1</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Laws of Testimony &mdash; 1<br>Based on Likutay Moharan I:66</div>
</header>

<p>
<span class="scripture">&ldquo;By the mouth of two witnesses&hellip; a matter shall be established&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 19:15)</span>: For the witnesses reveal the truth, and through this they raise the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> from its fall. For through the witnesses, the judgment is made &mdash; which is the aspect of raising <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>. For the essential cause of its fall was through falsehood and strife, as above (in Hilchos Da&rsquo;yonim, Siman 1). And through truth comes its ascent, as is known &mdash; that the essential elevation and completeness of the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> is through the aspect of truth.
</p>

<p>
And therefore there must be <span class="precise">specifically</span> two witnesses. For the blemish of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, is the corruption of Creation. For the essential Creation and governance of the world is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, as is known. And all of this [corruption] is brought about through the falsehood and strife &mdash; which are the evil and the impurity &mdash; through which the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> is blemished, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>. For there is the essential hold [of the <em>k&rsquo;lipos</em>], and through them Creation is corrupted, as above. For <span class="scripture">&ldquo;upon three things the world stands: upon justice, upon truth, and upon peace&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Avos 1:18)</span>. And when there is no truth and peace, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, the world is blemished and corrupted.
</p>

<p>
And these two witnesses, who come to reveal the truth and to raise <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> as above &mdash; they are the sustenance of the world, and they build the world anew. For the essential building and sustenance of the world is through truth, as above. For the seal of the Holy One, Blessed is He, is truth, and through it He created the world, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Who created you, Yaakov&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 43:1)</span>. And our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;My world, My world! Who created you? Yaakov created you!&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Bereishis Rabbah; Zohar)</span>. Yaakov &mdash; this is the aspect of truth, as is explained: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Give truth to Yaakov&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Michah 7:20)</span>. As Rabbainu, <em>zichrono livrachah</em>, wrote.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of two witnesses, based on what Rabbainu, <em>zichrono livrachah</em>, wrote (Siman 66): that before the Creation, the potential <span class="key-term-def">[<em>koach</em>]</span> and the actual <span class="key-term-def">[<em>po&rsquo;al</em>]</span> were together, and there was no distinction between them. And afterward they were opened, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;You open Your hand&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 145:16)</span> &mdash; a <em>yud</em> at the beginning and a <em>yud</em> at the end. And this is the aspect of bringing forth from potential to actual, which is the aspect of Creation. And all of this is done through speech, which is done through the aspect of truth, as is written there.
</p>

<p>
Thus we find that the essential Creation &mdash; that is, bringing forth from potential to actual &mdash; is through the aspect of truth, as above. For the essential Creation is through truth. And therefore these witnesses, who come to reveal the truth and to raise <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, to rectify the Creation &mdash; they are two, in the aspect of a <em>yud</em> at the beginning and a <em>yud</em> at the end, the aspect of potential and actual. For through the truth that they reveal, they bring forth from potential to actual, as above &mdash; through which the Creation is rectified, as above.
</p>

<p>
For through the falsehood and strife that was caused between the litigants, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> was blemished, and the Creation was corrupted &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">sof hama&rsquo;aseh</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the end of action]</span>, the aspect of the actual. And it is known that at the time of blemish, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, the life-force ascends and withdraws upward, and then the end of action returns and ascends into the beginning of thought. And this is the corruption of the Creation, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em> &mdash; for it returns to the state before Creation, where the potential and actual are together, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore two witnesses are needed, who come and make known the truth, and through this they bring forth from potential to actual. And this is the aspect of two witnesses &mdash; the aspect of the two <em>yuds</em>, which are the aspect of potential and actual, as above. And through this, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> is rectified &mdash; the aspect of Creation, as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<p>
As it is found in the Tikkunim, that every person has two witnesses each day to testify to His unity, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> &mdash; namely, the sign of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillin</span> and the sign of the <span class="key-term">bris</span>, and on Shabbos, the sign of Shabbos etc. And they are in the aspect of the two aforementioned <em>yuds</em> of the two Names <span class="key-term">Y-A-H-D-O-N-H-Y</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the interleaving of the Names Havayah and Adnus]</span>.
</p>

<p>
Thus we find that the two witnesses are in the aspect of the two aforementioned <em>yuds</em>. For these witnesses too testify to His G-dliness and His unity, <span class="key-term">Yisborach Sh&rsquo;mo</span>. For they reveal the truth, which is the aspect of His unity and His G-dliness, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>. For the seal of the Holy One, Blessed is He, is truth, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Jeremiah 10:10)</span>. And <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem <em>Elokim</em>&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of the two <em>yuds</em>, the aspect of potential and actual. For <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem&rdquo;</span> &mdash; this is the aspect of the Name <span class="key-term">Havayah</span>, which is a <em>yud</em> at the beginning. And <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>Elokim</em>&rdquo;</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of a <em>yud</em> at the end, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Adnus</span>. And through truth they bring forth from potential to actual and reveal His G-dliness in the world. For the essential Creation was <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;in order that they should know Him.&rdquo;</span>
</p>

<p>
Thus we find that the two witnesses are in the aspect of the two witnesses that every person has &mdash; which are the two aforementioned signs [<span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillin</span> and <span class="key-term">bris</span>] &mdash; who testify to His G-dliness and to the renewal of the world, that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> brought everything forth from potential to actual. For the aforementioned signs &mdash; which are the sign of Shabbos, <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillin</span>, etc. &mdash; testify to this as well.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;By the mouth of two witnesses a matter shall be established&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 19:15)</span>. <span class="scripture">&ldquo;A matter shall be established&rdquo;</span> <span class="precise">specifically</span> &mdash; for they sustain and raise <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">davar</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;matter&rdquo; / &ldquo;word&rdquo;]</span>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;one leader for a generation&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Sanhedrin 8a)</span>, as Rabbainu, <em>zichrono livrachah</em>, wrote (Siman 4).
</p>

<p>
And this is <span class="precise">specifically</span> <span class="scripture">&ldquo;by the mouth of two&rdquo;</span> witnesses &mdash; <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>pi sh&rsquo;nayim</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;the mouth of two&rdquo; / &ldquo;a double portion&rdquo;]</span> specifically &mdash; the aspect of the speech of truth, which is called <span class="key-term">pi sh&rsquo;nayim</span>. For it is comprised of the two aforementioned spirits [potential and actual]. For through it they bring forth from potential to actual. And therefore speech in <span class="key-term">Lashon HaKodesh</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the Holy Tongue]</span> is called <span class="key-term">pi sh&rsquo;nayim</span>, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Let there be, I pray, a double portion of your spirit&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">(II Kings 2:9)</span>. And as was explained above in Hilchos T&rsquo;rumos, Halachah 1; see there. And therefore two witnesses are needed, for through the aspect of <span class="key-term">pi sh&rsquo;nayim</span>, through this they bring forth from potential etc., and the Creation is rectified &mdash; which is the aspect of raising <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a matter shall be established,&rdquo;</span> as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<p>
And therefore one witness alone is invalid for testimony, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;One witness shall not rise up&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 19:15)</span>. And even if he is like Moshe Rabbainu, <em>alav hashalom</em>, he may not testify [alone]. For there is no power to bring forth from potential to actual and to raise <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> except through <span class="key-term">pi sh&rsquo;nayim</span>, which is the aspect of the two <em>yuds</em>, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore the witnesses are forbidden to be relatives of one another. For when they are relatives, they are from the root of a single point, and then even though they are two or more, they are not reckoned as more than one. For they must <span class="precise">specifically</span> be in the aspect of two points &mdash; the aspect of potential and actual. And therefore, when they are distant from one another, each one has a point unto himself.
</p>

<p>
And therefore, when they are two [unrelated witnesses], they are always in the aspect of an upper point and a lower point. For no two people are equal, and each one is in the aspect of an upper point relative to his fellow. And as is found in the teaching <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And you shall be unto Me a kingdom&rdquo;</span> etc. (Siman 34): that every person of Yisroel has a point that his fellow does not have, and his fellow needs to receive from that point. Thus he is, regarding that point, in the aspect of a <span class="key-term">rav</span> <span class="key-term-def">[teacher]</span> relative to his fellow, and his fellow is in the aspect of a <span class="key-term">talmid</span> <span class="key-term-def">[student]</span> who needs to receive from him. And <em>rav</em> and <em>talmid</em> &mdash; they are the aspect of the two aforementioned points, which are the aspect of the two <em>yuds</em>, the aspect of potential and actual, as above &mdash; the aspect of an upper point and a lower point.
</p>

<p>
And therefore converts who converted have no [halakhic] kinship, even two brothers etc. &mdash; for <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;a convert who converted is like a newborn child&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Yevamos 22a)</span>. For a convert does not receive his holy point &mdash; that is, his <span class="key-term">neshamah</span> &mdash; from the side of his family at the time of his birth, for they are uncircumcised. He only receives his point at the time that he converts. And therefore he is like a newborn child. And therefore, even though in nature they are brothers and relatives, nevertheless, since from the standpoint of the [holy] point they have no kinship, they are therefore valid to testify [together]. For each one has a point unto himself, which they received at the time they converted. And the essential [power of] testimony is only through the aspect of the points, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">pi sh&rsquo;nayim</span>, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore those who are disqualified through transgression are invalid to testify. For it is found there in the aforementioned teaching that transgression comes through the blemish and the fall of the hands, which is the aspect of the two aforementioned <em>yuds</em>; see there. And therefore he is invalid to testify, for the essential [power of] testimony is through the aspect of the two aforementioned <em>yuds</em>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">pi sh&rsquo;nayim</span>, as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&diams; &diams; &diams; &diams; &diams;</div>

<!-- ====== TRANSLATOR SUMMARY ====== -->
<div class="translator-summary">
<h3>Translator&rsquo;s Summary &mdash; Hilchos Eidus 1</h3>

<p>
Based on Likutay Moharan I:66. This halachah is a single, continuous text without <em>osiyos</em> divisions. Its central argument: <strong>witnesses reveal truth, and truth sustains the world</strong>. The blemish of <em>Malchus</em> (= the corruption of Creation) comes through falsehood and strife; witnesses who reveal the truth reverse this, raising <em>Malchus</em> from its fall.
</p>

<p>
The key mystical mechanism: Rabbainu teaches (Siman 66) that before Creation, <em>koach</em> (potential) and <em>po&rsquo;al</em> (actual) were fused together. Creation = bringing forth from potential to actual, represented by two <em>yuds</em> &mdash; one at the beginning, one at the end (from <em>&ldquo;Pose&rsquo;ach es yadecha&rdquo;</em>). This is done through the speech of truth. When falsehood corrupts the world, <em>sof hama&rsquo;aseh</em> (the actual) collapses back into <em>t&rsquo;chilas hamachshavah</em> (the potential) &mdash; a reversion to the pre-Creation state. Two witnesses, through revealing truth, re-enact Creation itself by bringing forth from potential to actual again.
</p>

<p>
This framework explains multiple halachos of testimony: (1) why two witnesses are required &mdash; the two <em>yuds</em> of <em>koach</em> and <em>po&rsquo;al</em>; (2) why <em>&ldquo;yakum davar&rdquo;</em> = raising <em>Malchus</em> (= <em>davar</em>); (3) why <em>&ldquo;pi sh&rsquo;nayim&rdquo;</em> = speech that contains two &ldquo;spirits&rdquo;; (4) why relatives are invalid &mdash; they share a single root-point, so they count as one rather than two; (5) why even Moshe cannot testify alone; (6) why converts have no halakhic kinship for testimony (each receives a new point at conversion); (7) why transgressors are invalid (they blemish the &ldquo;hands&rdquo; = the two <em>yuds</em>). Each person in Yisroel has a unique point his fellow lacks (Siman 34), making every pair an &ldquo;upper point / lower point&rdquo; = <em>rav</em> and <em>talmid</em> = <em>koach</em> and <em>po&rsquo;al</em>.
</p>

<p class="translator-note">
&mdash; Translator&rsquo;s summary. Not part of the original text.<br>
End of Hilchos Eidus 1.
</p>
